<title>PORTUGAL: Trade resumes in Reditus.</title>
<headline>Trade resumes in Reditus.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Financial Markets Committee has lifted the suspension in trade of shares of Portuguese computer group Reditus, market sources said.</p>
<p>The Financial Markets Committee (CMVM) suspended trade in Reditus shares on Thursday after a press report said offshore company Greenville Securities Ltd planned to take a stake of more than 25 percent in the company.</p>
<p>Reditus said it had set a meeting with Greenville for March 3 at which Greenville will discuss the possibility of taking a stake in Reditus.</p>
<p>Reditus traded at 652 escudos, up 102, at 1144 GMT after the suspension was lifted.</p>
